{"id": "q0353", "pool": "easy-fact", "tier": "aggressive", "audio_s": 3.9, "n_chunks": 4, "n_concurrent": 4, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.3616, "eot_read_ms": 23, "reference_answer": "The Fates", "query": "Who were the Greek equivalents of the Norns of Norse mythology?", "transcript": "Who are the Greek equivalents of the Norns of Norse mythology?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "The Greek equivalents of the Norns are the **Moirai**, or **Fates**. They control destiny much like the Norns, with each sister representing a different aspect of life's thread—spinning it, measuring it, and ultimately cutting it to end life.", "expert_answer": "The Greek equivalents of the Norns are the **Moirai**, or **Fates**:\n\n- **Clotho** — spins the thread of life  \n- **Lachesis** — measures the thread  \n- **Atropos** — cuts the thread, ending life", "expert_latency_s": 2.17, "stall_ms": 28, "relay_ms": 1520}
