{"id": "q0410", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "aggressive", "audio_s": 0.91, "n_chunks": 1, "n_concurrent": 1, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2615, "eot_read_ms": 27, "reference_answer": null, "query": "What is fleece?", "transcript": "What is fleece?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Fleece is a soft, warm fabric with a fuzzy or brushed surface. It is commonly made from synthetic fibers like polyester and is used for jackets, blankets, sweatshirts, and outdoor clothing because it is lightweight, insulating, and quick-drying. \"Fleece\" can also refer to the woolly coat of a sheep or similar animal before it is processed into yarn or fabric.", "expert_answer": "Fleece is a soft, warm fabric with a fuzzy or brushed surface. It is commonly made from synthetic fibers like polyester and is used for jackets, blankets, sweatshirts, and outdoor clothing because it is lightweight, insulating, and quick-drying.\n\n“Fleece” can also refer to the woolly coat of a sheep or similar animal before it is processed into yarn or fabric.", "expert_latency_s": 2.57, "stall_ms": 27, "relay_ms": 2167}
{"id": "q0423", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "aggressive", "audio_s": 2.1, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2512, "eot_read_ms": 22, "reference_answer": null, "query": "What services does Microsoft offer?", "transcript": "What services does Microsoft offer?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Microsoft offers a wide range of technology products and services, including cloud computing through Azure, productivity software like Microsoft 365, operating systems such as Windows, business applications in the Dynamics 365 suite, developer tools, AI services, gaming platforms with Xbox, cybersecurity solutions, hardware like Surface devices, and various enterprise services for businesses.", "expert_answer": "Microsoft offers a wide range of technology products and services, including:\n\n- **Cloud computing:** Microsoft Azure, cloud storage, databases, AI services, virtual machines\n- **Productivity software:** Microsoft 365, Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook, Teams\n- **Operating systems:** Windows for PCs, servers, and enterprise environments\n- **Business applications:** Dynamics 365 for CRM, ERP, finance, sales, and customer service\n- **Developer tools:** Visual Studio, GitHub, .NET, Azure DevOps\n- **AI services:** Copilot, Azure OpenAI Service, machine learning tools\n- **Gaming:** Xbox consoles, Xbox Game Pass, Xbox Cloud Gaming, game studios\n- **Cybersecurity:** Microsoft Defender, Sentinel, Entra identity services\n- **Hardware:** Surface laptops/tablets, accessories, Xbox hardware\n- **Enterprise services:** Consulting, support, cloud migration, compliance, and IT management tools", "expert_latency_s": 4.2, "stall_ms": 27, "relay_ms": 1877}
{"id": "q0430", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "aggressive", "audio_s": 2.4, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.0827, "eot_read_ms": 17, "reference_answer": null, "query": "Why do people like to buy Apple products?", "transcript": "Why do people like to buy Apple products?", "mode": "local", "answer": "People like to buy Apple products because they are known for being high quality, reliable, and easy to use. Many people also enjoy the design of Apple products—they look sleek and modern. Plus, Apple makes everything work together nicely, like phones, computers, and music players. People often feel that using Apple products helps them stay organized and connected in a simple way.", "answer_ms": 1843}
{"id": "q0445", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "aggressive", "audio_s": 1.94, "n_chunks": 2, "n_concurrent": 2, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.4887, "eot_read_ms": 23, "reference_answer": null, "query": "Who invented Boltzmann Machines?", "transcript": "Who invented Boltzmann machines?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Boltzmann machines were introduced by **David Ackley, Geoffrey Hinton, and Terrence Sejnowski** in 1985.", "expert_answer": "Boltzmann machines were introduced by **David Ackley, Geoffrey Hinton, and Terrence Sejnowski** in 1985.", "expert_latency_s": 3.57, "stall_ms": 27, "relay_ms": 874}
{"id": "q0456", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "aggressive", "audio_s": 1.82, "n_chunks": 2, "n_concurrent": 2, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.0586, "eot_read_ms": 23, "reference_answer": null, "query": "How can I sleep well at night?", "transcript": "How can I sleep well at night?", "mode": "local", "answer": "To sleep well at night, try keeping a regular sleep schedule by going to bed and waking up at the same time every day. Create a calming bedtime routine, like reading or taking a warm bath. Make your bedroom comfortable—cool, quiet, and dark—and limit screen time before bed. Avoid caffeine and heavy meals close to bedtime. If you're still having trouble, consider talking to a healthcare professional. Sweet dreams!", "answer_ms": 2235}
{"id": "q0462", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "aggressive", "audio_s": 2.25, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1846, "eot_read_ms": 23, "reference_answer": null, "query": "What is the best watch in the world ?", "transcript": "What is the best watch in the world?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "There isn't one universally \"best\" watch in the world—it depends on what you value. For prestige and collecting, Patek Philippe is often considered top-tier. For everyday luxury or durability, Rolex and Casio G-Shock have strong followings. If you're into high-end craftsmanship, brands like A. Lange & Söhne or Vacheron Constantin are highly respected. And for smart features, the Apple Watch Ultra stands out. Ultimately, the \"best\" watch is the one that fits your lifestyle and preferences.", "expert_answer": "There isn’t one universally “best” watch in the world—it depends on what you value:\n\n- **Best prestige/collecting:** Patek Philippe  \n- **Best everyday luxury:** Rolex  \n- **Best high-end craftsmanship:** A. Lange & Söhne or Vacheron Constantin  \n- **Best value mechanical:** Grand Seiko  \n- **Best durability:** Casio G-Shock  \n- **Best smartwatch:** Apple Watch Ultra  \n\nIf forced to name one overall “best” traditional watch brand, many collectors would say **Patek Philippe**.", "expert_latency_s": 7.1, "stall_ms": 28, "relay_ms": 3022}
{"id": "q0469", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "aggressive", "audio_s": 3.41, "n_chunks": 4, "n_concurrent": 4, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1028, "eot_read_ms": 23, "reference_answer": null, "query": "What are some silly things to drink out of instead of a cup?", "transcript": "What are some silly things to drink out of instead of a cup?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Sure! Here are some silly things to drink out of instead of a cup:\\n\\n1. A tiny teacup on top of your head.\\n2. A giant hollowed-out pickle.\\n3. A mason jar shaped like a dinosaur.\\n4. A bowl turned upside down.\\n5. A paper bag with a straw poking out.\\n6. A balloon filled with air and tied at the bottom.\\n7. A tiny boot or shoe.\\n8. A stack of pancakes with a hole in the middle.\\n9. A plastic toy truck.\\n10. A hat with a hidden opening.\\n\\nHave fun experimenting!", "answer_ms": 3772}
